.TH TFORMAT 1.SH NAMEtformat \- fill and justify text.SH SYNOPSIS\fBtformat\fR[width] < infile > outfile.SH DESCRIPTION\fBtformat\fRreads text on the standard input and writes it refilled to\fIwidth\fRcolumns, 80 unless told, each line justified to both margins byspreading the spaces.  A blank line ends a paragraph.  Spaces at thestart of a paragraph are kept as its indent..PPA line beginning with a dot is a command, not text:.TP 12\fB.c\fRthe rest of the line, centred..TP 12\fB.b\fR.TP 12\fB.s\fRa blank line..PPOther dot lines are ignored..SH EXAMPLES.nftformat 60 < draft > finalrstory | tformat.fi.SH NOTESOne of Robert Heller's programs translated from SNOBOL4 into C, fromJames F. Gimpel's\fIAlgorithms in SNOBOL4\fR;\fR\fBDOC/snobol\fRdescribes the set and\fBSRC/effo_snobol\fRholds the source..SH SEE ALSOfmt, proff, nroff